    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "DNG Royal County, Navan`s premier estate agents, are delighted to present 59 Canterbrook, Trim Road, Navan, Co. Meath, a beautifully maintained and generously proportioned three/four-bedroom semi-detached house for sale in the popular Canterbrook development.\n\n\nExtending to approximately 108 sq.m, this spacious family home offers a well-balanced and versatile layout, with the added benefit of an additional ground-floor room suitable as a fourth bedroom, family room, home office or playroom.\n\nThe accommodation opens with a bright entrance hall leading to a spacious living room with a large bay window, allowing plenty of natural light to fill the room. The open-plan kitchen and dining area overlooks the rear garden, with sliding patio doors providing direct access outside. Just off the kitchen is a separate utility room with access to the garden, together with a guest W.C.\n\nUpstairs, there are three generously proportioned bedrooms, including the main bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the generous rear garden is laid mainly in lawn and enjoys the evening sun, providing an ideal space for outdoor dining and family life. To the front, a cobblelock driveway provides ample off-street parking, complemented by a neatly maintained lawn and mature feature tree.\n\nCanterbrook is a popular and well-established residential development situated just off the Trim Road in Navan, Co. Meath. No. 59 is within walking distance of Beechmount Shopping Centre and Navan Town Centre, with a wide range of schools, shops, sporting facilities and local amenities close by.\n\nThe area is well served by public transport and offers convenient access to the M3 motorway, providing easy connectivity to Dublin and the surrounding areas.\n\nWith its generous accommodation, versatile layout, attractive rear garden and convenient location, No. 59 is an ideal family home with plenty to offer.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment with DNG Royal County."
      },
      {
